  "findings": [
    "AY/YM generator, JT03/FM implementation and mixer are identical to pinned TSConf. Imported TurboSound only ties unused IO input pins to FF.",
    "BaseConf uses the same 28.0303 MHz domain and divide-by-eight PSG master enable. Its combinational enable is one bus cycle out of phase with the registered TSConf enable, without a rate change.",
    "Both ports use the same final mixer. ADC/ESP mixer branches are disabled in the BaseConf Mini synthesis configuration.",
    "Mini analog sigma-delta input differs: BaseConf uses full 16-bit offset-binary while TSConf right-shifts by two and discards two more low bits. This is roughly 4x DAC input gain, but is not on HDMI or Mini G.",
    "Mini G I2S divider and HDMI sample handoff match the reference structure. HDMI and analog consume the same mixer signal.",
    "All 18 CPU-driven AY/YM tests pass: 3 targets x 3 CPU speeds x 2 chip types. Register readback on both chips, distinct stereo fixed levels, and noise-disabled ~438 Hz tone have expected samples and exact periods."
  ],
